## 10. Testing and Completion Criteria

We will test the project in stages.

### Database

- All migrations run successfully.
- Foreign keys and unique constraints work.
- Seeders can be rerun safely where appropriate.
- `php artisan migrate:fresh --seed` succeeds in the development/test environment.

### Allocation

- CL and SL are not granted on joining.
- First allocation occurs after one year.
- CL carry-forward is capped at 5 days.
- SL does not carry forward.
- LWP limit is enforced.
- WFH is allocated after 6 years according to its rule.
- Expired grants cannot be used.
- Scheduled allocations do not duplicate grants.

### Applications and approvals

- One pending application per employee.
- Overlapping approved leave is rejected.
- Insufficient balance is rejected.
- Rejection requires a reason.
- Only authorized approvers can decide.
- The first decision finalizes the outcome.
- Cancellation preserves history.

### Attendance and consistency

- Approved leave updates attendance.
- Pending/rejected leave does not appear as approved leave.
- Weekly offs and holidays are excluded from deductions.
- Attendance is unique per employee/date.
- Failed approval processing rolls back related changes.
- Administrator cancellation restores the correct balance and attendance.

### Project delivery

- Models and relationships are documented.
- Seed data supports testing.
- Automated tests cover important rules.
- README explains setup, migrations, seeders, scheduled tasks, and tests.
- Changes are committed in small, task-focused commits.
